      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is literally my most requested feature to add out of the 20+ mods I use to run. \nIt enables me to go from sub 10fps in club worlds / large gatherings to over 40, and it's better than the safety feature of turning everyone into robots because robots are just not fun to look at, they're just not. I can have everyone's base model shown in my safety settings, and only when I come into distance with them do I render their avatar at all. Meaning I don't have to constantly fiddle with settings, allowing avatars etc, when I move around / change worlds just in order to see them. It's also incredibly useful if you want to sit at the back of a club / large group of people and see through them, only viewing the performers at the front, as anyone past the set distance doesn't render.\nIt has no negative affects for VRC, hiding someone else's avatar doesn't cause a detriment to game worlds / other people in any way, if anything it would just hurt you.\nThis is what this feature needs:\n- It needs to have a variable distance slider / numeric input.\n- Always show the nameplates, even when the avatar is hidden.\n- The hidden avatars are still selectable / hearable, etc. It's just the rendering of the model that is stopped.\n- Showing avatars will bypass the distance based hiding\n- Ability to allow friends to bypass distance based hiding",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
