      "value": "@{60cb78838b5c3f1e8f8fddf1|full_name}: Yes, this exactly. Everything you said. This one basic, no-brainer, easy to implement feature singlehandedly MAKES the difference between whether public worlds and especially clubs are only viable for people with very high-end PCs (current situation), vs. open to most everyone.\nMy system isn't even a potato. It's actually very powerful. But not powerful enough to show more than just my friends at a club. I'm currently stranded in the middle of nowhere (super rural area), transitioning, and recovering from a debilitating injury, and I love music. I really need to be able to meet new people in clubs. That's way way harder to do if I don't even get to really see any strangers without showing their avatars one by one and being careful to hide anyone I'm not still talking to (so that I don't end up showing too many at once). I had this already solved before the crazy devs decided to take away functionality like this that so many of us depend on, instead of implementing it BEFORE implementing EAC. Y'all need to rush this out ASAP if you're really committed to EAC now.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
